  "id": "Compound::DB00509 - Gene::28231",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset suggests a potential relationship between Dextrothyroxine and Slco4a1, mediated through Levothyroxine. Dextrothyroxine is linked to several conditions, including craniosynostosis, slipped femoral capital epiphysis, and epiphysiolysis, all of which are associated with Levothyroxine. Levothyroxine is known to bind to Slco4a1, a protein involved in drug transport and metabolism. This indicates that Dextrothyroxine may influence the activity of Slco4a1 through the intermediary of Levothyroxine. The shared pathway involving Thyroxine and Thyroid Agent as lowest common ancestors further supports a systemic interaction between Dextrothyroxine and Levothyroxine, which in turn affects Slco4a1. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, though not fully understood, mechanism by which Dextrothyroxine may modulate Slco4a1 function. The evidence highlights a possible regulatory role of Dextrothyroxine in the transport or metabolism of Slco4a1, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
